-- A threshold pressure between two equilibration regions in a compositional
-- run.  The column of MULTZ_BARRIER without the barrier: 20 cells split into
-- two blocks of ten, each its own equilibration region, the upper block
-- equilibrated at 250 bar and the lower at 155 bar, each with a water zone at
-- its base.
--
-- THPRES lets fluid cross the region boundary only where the potential
-- difference exceeds 50 bar, and reduces the difference by that amount.
-- Layer 10 at the base of the upper block holds water and layer 11 at the top
-- of the lower block holds hydrocarbon, so water flows down across the
-- boundary, and the hydrocarbon would have to flow against the potential
-- difference to cross upwards.  The upper block loses pressure and the lower
-- block gains it until, within the first two report steps, the potential
-- difference of about 98 bar has fallen to 50 bar.  The water that crossed
-- stays in layer 11, below the critical water saturation, and both blocks are
-- at rest from then on.  Without THPRES the blocks equalise within the first
-- report step.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
   A 50 BAR THRESHOLD PRESSURE BETWEEN TWO COMPOSITIONAL BLOCKS

METRIC

TABDIMS
/
OIL
GAS
WATER
DIMENS
1 1 20 /

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP /

START
  1 'JAN' 2016  /

REGDIMS
1 1 0 0 /

EQLDIMS
2 200 /

EQLOPTS
'THPRES' /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

------------------------------------------------------------------------
GRID
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/grid.inc' /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROPS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/props.inc' /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
REGIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
EQLNUM
10*1 10*2
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOLUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The water-oil contact of each block lies three layers above its base.
EQUIL
   2010  250  2035  0  2000  0  /
   2060  155  2085  0  2050  0  /

-- Flow between the regions needs a potential difference above 50 bar.
THPRES
 1 2 50.0 /
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/summary.inc' /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCHEDULE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/schedule.inc' /

END
